HIRD hand-written amend mechanism (amend_source, amend_extraction, this), each with its own argument names and none sharing a ledger. Fix: one amend(table, key, field, value, reason) whose amendable set is derived per table, per (1). ALSO OWED: walk.py is cited by a checked-in workplan as its rule-7a generator but lives under scratchpad/, which schema_reference_audit SKIPs and derived_not_curated_audit''s WRITER_ROOTS excludes -- it names ~30 tables and columns in raw SQL, so a rename sweeps every other reader and leaves it silently broken, which is rule 4''s exact failure mode. It was NOT moved to scripts/ here because an unregistered executable under scripts/ is itself the defect rule 8 names; the move and the check-registry entry are one job, not two.', '2026-09-18 05:11', 'session_2026-09-18-research-batch-15-t2-synthesis-threshold', '2026-09-18 05:11', 'session_2026-09-18-research-batch-15-t2-synthesis-threshold', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);